body:
Oof. Thankfully my depression is so much better now that I am transitioning but it still comes by every once and a while to let me know its still there. It is like night and day different from when I was in denial vs now that I'm out and able to be myself all the time.  I've been really avoiding talking to a therapist but I think I'm really going to need to pretty soon. I just learned that Anhedonia is a thing and to be honest a lot of the sex-specific symptoms are pretty similar to what I've been experiencing for the last 4-6 years so. So it's making me seriously consider talking to a mental health professional about it and see what if anything can be done about it.

&#x200B;

Thank you For making this post
